From tru64-unix-managers  Thu Jul 23 00:07:49 1998
From: Ian Mortimer <ian () physics ! uq ! edu ! au>
Date: Thu, 23 Jul 1998 00:07:49 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: [SUMMARY] UPS for PW 500au
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96078715811865

Hi All

My question was:

   Any recommendations for a reliable, fairly low cost UPS that will work 
   with DU 4.0[cd] on a PW 500au?  Negative recommendations also welcome.

Thanks to Eric Sven Ristad, Colin Brooks, Tom Webster and 
Claudia A T C Burg for their replies.

Eric recommended the Exide Powerware Prestige series which comes
with software that runs under Digital Unix.  He did say they were
expensive though.

Colin and Claudia both recommended APC SmartUPS - Colin has a
1400 which is bigger than we need and Claudia has a 1000 which
is closer to the mark.

Tom recommended either APC or Best power but his warning about
hidden costs associated with the APC range is worth repeating:

> A UPS from either APC or Best power should work fine.  APC (www.apcc.com)
> is the better known company, but keep in mind you will need to buy 
> shutdown software and a special cable to use the UPS with DU, this runs
> about US$150.  Best (www.bestpower.com) includes the cable and portable
> UPS software on CDROM with the UPS.
> 
> I personally prefer Best, it's mostly because Best is up-front with the
> pricing (rather than hitting you up for more money for software and 
> cables).  If you are looking at running multiple systems off of one
> UPS, APC has some interesting hardware solutions to the problem.

Best Power's Australian distributor is Sola (www.solaaust.com.au)
so I'll be checking out their range as well as the APC and 
Exide ranges.


Ian

