Subject: SUMMARY: CDE Login Banner
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96078715811781


Thanks to the following for their replies,

Chad Price
Richard Tome
Tom Woodburn
and in particular to Ron Bowman.

The problem is that in the Xresources file, !! is a comment delimiter.

The procedure for changing the banner is as follows:

check for the existence of the directory /etc/dt/config/C.  If it doesn't   
exist, then create it using mkdir -p  /etc/dt/config/C

Copy the file /usr/dt/config/C/Xresource to /etc/dt/config/C

Copy the file /usr/dt/config/Xconfig to /etc/dt/config

Edit Xresources changing the entry for Dtlogin*greeting...  to the text   
you require.  - Don't forget to remove the comments.

Edit Xconfig and change the entry:  Xconfig:Dtlogin*resources:   
            %L/Xresources

to: Xconfig:Dtlogin*resources:             /etc/dt/config/C/Xresources

There should be no need to restart xlogin.  Either log out and the new   
banner will show, or use the reset login on the login screen.

For those that mentioned /etc/issue,  on the first couple of lines appear   
in a popup.  You have to clear the popup to enter you login name.


