Content-Transfer-Encoding: 7bit

     Hi, managers.
     
     The problem, I reported was that in a cluster, I suddenly got a lot of 
     errors in the uerf log referring to disks that other members of the 
     cluster had mounted.
     
     Almost all agreed that this was caused by 'advfsd' that monitors care 
     of the file sets and domains. This program makes a sort of 'scu show 
     edt' and monitors all the disks found here. But some of those are 
     reserved by other members of the cluster and that causes the error. 
     
     Chris H Ruhnke suggested that one could put the names of the disks 
     mounted by other cluster members into a 'ignore' file (THANKS!!, it is 
     not documented in the man pages) and then restart advfsd. That seems 
     to work quite well with the following to note:
     
        On my system (DU4.0D patch kit 1):
                It is /var/opt/... instead of /usr/opt/...
                It doesn't seem necessary to restart advfsd.
     
     I attach an awk script that I have made that can be run by cron. It 
     makes an ignore file that contains those disks of the disks visible by 
     scu that are not below /etc/fdmns.
     
     
     Thanks to 
     
     + Chris H Ruhnke who suggested changing /usr/opt/advfsd/disks.ignore
     + Mike Cross
     + Viktor Holmberg
     + Steve Parker
     + rye@jtasc.acom.mil
     + Rodrigo Poblete
     + Ken Krueger



--simple boundary
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=US-ASCII; name="ignore~1.awk"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 7bit
Content-Disposition: attachment; filename="ignore~1.awk"

#!/usr/bin/awk -f
BEGIN	{	while ("/sbin/scu show edt" | getline ) {
			for (i=1; i <= NF; i++) {
				if ($(i-1) == "Bus:")
					bus=$i;
				if ($(i-1) == "Target:")
					target=$i;
				if ($(i-1) == "Lun:")
					lun=$i;
				if ($(i-1) == "Type:")
					type=$i;
			}
				
			if (type == "Direct") {
				sub(/,/, "", bus);
				sub(/,/, "", target);
				sub(/,/, "", lun);
				if (lun == 0)
					lunletter="";
				else if (lun == 1)
					lunletter="a";
				else if (lun == 2)
					lunletter="b";
				else if (lun == 3)
					lunletter="c";
				else if (lun == 4)
					lunletter="d";
				else if (lun == 5)
					lunletter="e";
				else if (lun == 6)
					lunletter="f";
				else if (lun == 7)
					lunletter="g";

				disk=sprintf("rz%c%d", lunletter, bus*8+target);
				alldisks[disk]=1;
			}
		}

		while ("find /etc/fdmns" | getline) {
			sub(/\/.*\//, "");
			sub(/.$/, "");
			if (alldisks[$1]) {
				alldisks[$1]=0;
			}
		}


		for (disk in alldisks) 
			if (alldisks[disk])
				print disk > "/var/opt/advfsd/disks.ignore";
	}


