Hi Gurus,

Many thanks for

Tim Ambrose <tim_ambrose@yahoo.com>
Robert Otterson <Robert.Otterson@digital.com>
Ram Nagpure <ramn@wipinfo.soft.net>

Tim's suggestion of checking the permissions of

/etc/svc.conf
/etc/resolv.conf

solved the problem. Apparently DU 4.0b Net Config GUI has a bug
that caused svc.config permissions and ownership be changed after
netmask reconfiguration. After moving to 755 bin bin and rebooting 
things are running smoothly now.


