From tru64-unix-managers  Fri Jul 03 18:36:43 1998
From: Jon Wright <jon.wright () ui ! com>
Date: Fri, 03 Jul 1998 18:36:43 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: SUMMARY: rz devices renumbered after system repaired by DEC
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96078715811487

The AlphaStation 600 has an I/O subsystem module which includes two
identical SCSI connectors. One connector goes to internal drives first and
then to a narrow (50-pin) high-density external connector. The second
connector goes directly to a wide (68-pin) high-density external connector.
The former is bus scsi0; the latter is bus scsi1.

Evidently when putting my system back together the Digital technician wired
the SCSI busses backwards. I opened the system up, swapped the SCSI cables
on the I/O subsystem module and just like magic, everything was back to
normal.

